<title>UK: IATA details top 25 cargo airlines for 1996.</title>
<headline>IATA details top 25 cargo airlines for 1996.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Federal Express held its top ranking position for carrying air cargo in 1996 on combined domestic and international flights as ranked by the International Air Transport Association(IATA) on the basis of scheduled freight tonnes carried.</p>
<p>The data is published in the latest issue of IATA's World Air Transport Statistics issued Friday.</p>
<p>Comparative rankings and tonnages for 1995 may differ from those issued in June 1996 due to subsequent adjustments. The top 25 carriers are:</p>
<p>   Ranking				Tonnage		Tonnage</p>
<p>  1996 '95				1996		   1995</p>
<p>    1  (1)  Federal Express	 3,773		  3,421</p>
<p>    2  (2)  UPS			 2,887		     na</p>
<p>    3  (3)  Lufthansa		 1,038		    979</p>
<p>    4  (4)  Korean Airlines	   932		    851</p>
<p>    5  (5)  Japan Airlines	    863		    838</p>
<p>    6  (6)  Northhwest Airlines     696		    719</p>
<p>    7  (7)  Air France		  683		    657</p>
<p>    8  (9)  Singapore		   651		    586</p>
<p>    9  (8)  American Airlines	 603		    638</p>
<p>    10 (10) KLM			   575		    551</p>
<p>    11 (13) Cathay Pacific	    568		    522</p>
<p>    12 (12) British Airways	   558		    524</p>
<p>    13 (11) United Airlines	   544		    529</p>
<p>    14 (14) All Nippon Airways	490		    464</p>
